  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}+x$ which is defined and continuous on the closed interval $[1,8].$ By filling the blank spaces in the sentence below, complete the statement of the intermediate value theorem:\n\n*If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{\u00a0________\u00a0}$ inclusively, then there exists a number $c\\in [1,8]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*",
  "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[1,8],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(1)$ and $f(8).$\n\nSince $f(1)=2$ and $f(8)=10$, we must have \n$k\\in [2,10].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$2$ and $10$\".",
